# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every host.
#
# A Windows checkout otherwise converts them to CRLF, and the tree is read as
# bytes by nearly everything that gates it: the formatters report every line as
# changed, `shellcheck` refuses a literal carriage return, the schema drift test
# finds every checked-in schema differing from what the types generate, and
# `rustfmt` refuses generated code. What decides whether a file is text is git's
# own detection, so an image stays the bytes it was committed as.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The real-print cases' G-code and frames are Git LFS objects: about 140 MB that
# only the paid real-print suite reads. `.lfsconfig` excludes them from every
# download, so a clone, a checkout, a pull and a new worktree carry these as
# pointers; `just real-prints-fetch` downloads them on purpose. Every other file
# of a case stays plain, and `just check-repo`'s `real-prints-lfs` refuses one
# of these committed as its raw bytes, which is what a host without git-lfs adds.
tests/real-prints/**/*.gcode filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
tests/real-prints/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
tests/real-prints/**/*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
tests/real-prints/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
